e often let her  temper get the better of her  and some officers saw this as an  opportunity to have it forcibly removed  from the organization  so they went out of their way to try and  provoke her  to them she was still the enemy who had  somehow managed to weasel away into the  mps  and could not be trusted she found  herself in a constant uphill battle  with every misstep and blunder being  highlighted and brought to her  superior's attention  yet she continued on she was there to do  a task  and to her it was much more than just a  job it was an opportunity to not just  dull the storm  but redirect it and heroes switching  sides didn't mean she wasn't still  protecting londoners from the racists  and agitators she was just executing it  from a different angle  and hopefully one that would have a  greater impact  as a street-hearted veteran she  certainly knew how to fight dirty  but the intention was so much more than  that and as one of the lead experts in  riot control  she brought in valuable knowledge to  scotland yard  eventually she graduated from hendon and  legitimately earned the respect of a  division and even the ones who had  initially opposed her  in 2011 class managed the front line of  the police territorial support group  and was an integral figure during the  london riots  it had begun during an initially  peaceful protest against the shooting by  the police  of a young man of mixed race  a number of rioters were motivated by  the anger and were against the brutal  treatment at the hands of the police  along with the grievances rising from  inequality and cuts to public services  the main responsibility during this riot  of the tsg and clash  was to stop the violence from spreading  to other districts and securing the  capital  while confronting the writers she had  once led and stood alongside  she was met with extreme hostility to  them  she was now the antagonist yet  undeterred  she held her ground alongside her fellow  tsg and proved once 